An MDI feed move (G1) must actually reach motion.

Regression test for a silent motion loss: a feed move leaves the naive-CAM
detector holding an open chain, nothing closed that chain at the end of an MDI
line, and the next MDI line's endpoint resync dropped it. G1 from MDI moved
nothing and reported success; G0 was unaffected because STRAIGHT_TRAVERSE
flushes the chain first.

Covers both MDI execution paths: a plain block (executeMDI) and the tail of an
o-word subroutine resumed after a queue buster (finishMDI's continuation loop,
which runs Interp::execute() with MDImode 0 and so never reaches the
interpreter's own canon.finish()).
